      "role": "user",
      "content": "I hear what you're saying about the 'practical function,' but it feels like you're framing the pro-testing side as the more established 'objective' view while the critiques are just part of a 'debate.' Given how much the research shows these tests correlate more with wealth and zip code than actual raw potential, isn't it more accurate to say that using them as a meritocratic tool is actually just a way to scientifically justify existing social hierarchies?",
